    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1567">

                <pb facs="1262" n="1146" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/408.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Government and both parties request supervision to include election for municipal
                    council to take place June 30 in all municipalities. Committee recommends it,
                    since otherwise this election will not be fair and disturbances may be
                    anticipated which will have a serious effect upon presidential electoral
                    situation. Referring to Department’s telegram of May 13, was this supervision
                    therein included?</p>
                <p>Registration is proceeding satisfactorily and will be concluded on June 15. Party
                    spirit remains high and numerous complaints of oppression and electoral
                    interference by Government officials, some of them corroborated by supervisors,
                    have been received from the Porras party. Committee has brought these to the
                    Government’s attention.</p>
                <p>Regarding Department’s telegram June 6, Chiarí exaggerating situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
